                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Killed or seriously injured. Police forces are moving to the injury-based CRASH system, which records more injuries as serious. DfT publishes the probability that each record would be 'serious' under injury-based reporting; KSI (adj) = fatal + that probability.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Rates are severity, not risk. ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "STATS19 has no traffic volumes, so a rate here is the severity of a collision given that it happened, not the risk per mile travelled.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Filters. ",
